<p><em>Whenever SCP-1525-2 decides to remove any article of clothing, they will immediately assume themselves to be fully unclothed.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is a key description, and a little confusing as it's phrased. Do you mean <em>after</em> they remove it? All their clothes, or one article? Or &#8230; while they're removing something?</p>
<p>I also think it would fledge out the weirdness-horror to list at least a few of the layers the first victim was wearing (like, &quot;ten pairs of socks, of various colors). Humorous and awful at the same time.</p>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> Actually, I'd almost think that &quot;upon waking the next day, regardless of what they are wearing&quot; they'll think they are naked, etc&#8212; would make more sense. Either that or &quot;upon fastening the watch&quot;, as the variation seems unnecessary/doesn't really add creepiness.</p>

							</div>

								
